      "extract": "[]{#sec:intro label=\"sec:intro\"} All graphs considered in this paper are finite and undirected with no loops or parallel edges. The order of a graph is meant to be its number of vertices. Denote by $A(\\Gamma)$ the adjacency matrix of a graph $\\Gamma$, and call its eigenvalues the *eigenvalues* of $\\Gamma$. Since $A(\\Gamma)$ is a real symmetric matrix, the eigenvalues of $\\Gamma$ are real numbers, and we order them",
